Overview
Context:
In the modern retail landscape, efficiency isn't just about profit—it's about sustainability. Every year, tons of fresh produce are wasted due to inaccurate demand forecasting. If a store overstocks, products expire on the shelf; if it understocks, it loses customers and revenue.

In this 5-hour intensive AI challenge, your mission is to build a high-precision Machine Learning model to predict the next two weeks daily demand for a national retail network.

The Challenge:
Participants will navigate a complex dataset that mirrors real-world market dynamics. To win, your model must decode how different contextual factors interact:

Temporal Context: what is the product sell through rate in the last period of time? how holidays influence the demand?

Spatial Context: How do store coordinates and local competition influence sales patterns?

Competitive Price Elasticity: How does demand shift when your price changes relative to nearby competitors?

New products: Special handling of recently-launched products with limited history.

